Keep the header on one line at phone width.

#topbar is a single flex row sized for a desktop — logo with tagline, search,
conversation totals, import, export, help — and there are no media queries. At
412px the tagline "every conversation, one map" wraps onto three lines and trebles
the row's height, and #counts, which is nowrap with margin-left:auto, pushes the
Export menu and the Help button clean off the right edge: measured at 383->443 and
449->465 in a 412px viewport.

Below 700px the tagline and the totals are hidden and the row's padding and gap
tighten, which leaves every control on one line with the search box free to take
the space the totals were using. The totals are the right thing to drop: the
sidebar already lists counts per provider, while Export is the only route to a
snapshot or to erasing local data. Nothing changes above 700px.

diff --git a/index.html b/index.html
index 7d7c140..92f08ed 100644
--- a/index.html
+++ b/index.html
@@ -49,6 +49,15 @@ input[type=checkbox]{accent-color:var(--accent);width:14px;height:14px}
   border-bottom:1px solid var(--sep)}
 #logo{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;font-size:13px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1px}
 #logo .sub{color:var(--label3);font-weight:400;font-size:11px}
+/* At phone width the header has room for the logo, search and the buttons, and
+   not much else. The tagline otherwise wraps to three lines and the totals, which
+   are nowrap and margin-left:auto, push Export and Help off the right edge. The
+   sidebar carries per-provider counts, so the totals are what gives way. */
+@media (max-width: 700px){
+  #logo .sub{display:none}
+  #counts{display:none}
+  #topbar{gap:6px;padding:0 8px}
+}
 #searchbox{flex:1;max-width:400px;position:relative;margin:0 4px}
 #search{width:100%;padding-left:26px;height:28px;border-radius:var(--r-field);font-size:13px}
 #search::placeholder{color:var(--label3)}
